  'storm-damage-knocks-out-power-pretoria-east-2026-11-26',
  'Storm damage knocks out power in parts of Pretoria East',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-26', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/26/hailstorm-batters-pretoria-leaving-damaged-homes-and-widespread-power-outages/',
  'A severe hailstorm on Wednesday damaged homes, trees and power lines across Pretoria East, and the city warned that repairs could take time.',
  'Severe thunderstorms brought hail, strong wind and heavy rain to Pretoria on Wednesday, after the South African Weather Service issued a level 4 warning covering Gauteng until midnight. Residents in several Pretoria East suburbs told Rekord of storm damage: trees came down in Faerie Glen, Lynnwood Glen and Die Wilgers, blocking roads and nearly flooding one home, while boundary walls collapsed at several properties in Olympus and a brick wall was damaged in Erasmuskloof. In La Montagne, fallen trees landed on perimeter walls and across a driveway.

The City of Tshwane said the storm had damaged electricity infrastructure in a number of areas, with uprooted trees and branches falling onto power lines. It said repair crews could only start work once conditions were safe, adding that how widespread the damage turned out to be would affect how soon power could return for households hit by the outages. EWN separately reported flooding and storm damage to homes, vehicles and roads in parts of Tshwane the following day, with the metro''s emergency services telling residents to stay clear of low-lying crossings, rivers and any spot where water had built up on roads.

Forecasters expect the unsettled weather to continue for a few more days. Showers and thundershowers were forecast through Thursday and Friday, with Saturday set to be the wettest day of the weekend before conditions ease on Sunday.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/26/hailstorm-batters-pretoria-leaving-damaged-homes-and-widespread-power-outages/", "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/26/joburg-motorists-urged-to-be-cautious-in-face-of-wet-weather-destructive-flooding"]',
  'agent'
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'moya-re-elected-tshwane-mayor-2026-11-26',
  'ActionSA''s Moya re-elected Tshwane mayor as new council sworn in',
  'Community', '2026-11-26', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-municipal-news/2026/11/26/tshwane-council-re-elects-moya-as-executive-mayor/',
  'Tshwane''s newly elected council re-elected ActionSA''s Nasiphi Moya as executive mayor on Thursday, beating the DA''s Cilliers Brink.',
  'Tshwane''s new municipal council was sworn in on Thursday, at its first sitting since the 4 November local government elections, and re-elected ActionSA''s Dr Nasiphi Moya as executive mayor for a further term. Moya won 115 of the votes cast against 87 for the DA''s Cilliers Brink, with seven ballots spoilt, according to Rekord''s count of the proceedings. The council has 214 seats, and the ANC-ActionSA-EFF coalition backing Moya controls 109 of them, meaning she drew extra support from outside that coalition to win.

The ANC''s Naeem Patel was elected council speaker, defeating the DA''s Pogiso Mthimunye and the VF Plus''s Willie Spies, while the EFF''s Omphile Maotwe was elected deputy mayor unopposed.

Moya''s return followed weeks of coalition talks after the DA won the most council seats in the election but fell short of a majority needed to govern alone. Rekord reported that talks between the DA and ActionSA broke down over how leadership positions in Johannesburg, Ekurhuleni and Tshwane would be shared, with each side rejecting the other''s proposal; Brink said afterwards that the DA would instead act as official opposition. ActionSA leader Herman Mashaba, reacting after the vote, called Moya''s re-election "a victory for the city''s residents" and said her return to office had now become real rather than just a goal the party was chasing.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-municipal-news/2026/11/26/tshwane-council-re-elects-moya-as-executive-mayor/", "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/26/da-bid-to-postpone-tshwane-mayoral-election-rejected-by-council-majority", "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/27/moya-s-re-election-as-tshwane-mayor-a-victory-for-residents-says-mashaba"]',
  'agent'
);
